Code Checker is a simple and interactive web application designed for writing, running, and testing Python code directly in the browser.

The website lets users paste Python code into a built-in editor, execute it instantly, and view the output in a dedicated output panel. It is ideal for beginners and learners who want to test small Python programs quickly without installing a local Python setup.

The project includes several useful features for code review and documentation. Users can run multiple code checks in a single session, track how many runs have been completed, clear the session history when needed, and export the complete record as either a PDF or a TXT file. The PDF export creates a clean report with headings, page breaks, and all saved input/output results from the current session, while the TXT export provides a simple plain-text version for easy sharing and storage.

The interface is clean, beginner-friendly, and responsive, making it easy to write code, check results, troubleshoot errors, and save work for later. This project demonstrates how HTML, CSS, and JavaScript can be combined to create a lightweight and practical coding tool for learning and experimentation.
